adr: 0344
file: lib/dialect/passortx.pas
kills: lib_sortx
why: SiftDown rises the *smaller* of the two children, so the heap property holds for one child and not the other and the sort delivers a permutation instead of an order. It is the classic heapsort defect and it is silent on short inputs -- the record's own point is that a library is where a generic routine is first used in anger, so the case that catches it is the client program and not a compiler test.
--- old
      if (child + 1 <= limit) and then before(a[child], a[child + 1]) then
        child := child + 1;
--- new
      if (child + 1 <= limit) and then before(a[child + 1], a[child]) then
        child := child + 1;
